{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/793341-gift-of-opening","id":793341,"title":"Gift of Opening","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-26T17:48:17-08:00","id":793341,"title":"Gift of Opening","content":"So I made a Gift of Opening for a player in my game for various reasons. I always liked the Lodge of Doors (and the 1e Gift of Opening) in concept if not execution. Right now the gift is very strong which I'm fine with but I'm just shooting for 'Not Gamebreaking' here.<br /> <br /> I'm having the most trouble with the Cunning Facet in its entirety (which is almost certainly the one he will be starting play with). I've toyed with increasing penalties and essence costs based on Sympathetic Connection (as seen in Mage). I've toyed with daily limits equal to Cunning, though I feel that destroys the fantasy of 'Blinking' a bit. The cost was recently 3 Essence with a distance of Cunning Renown x 100 yards, which I may or may not be going back to. Just trying to find a balance. I'm not sure if the ridiculous amount of modifiers/penalties I've added to it have done enough of the job yet and more eyes on it can't hurt.<br /> <br /> Other thoughts I am having:<ul><li>I <i>am </i>planning on putting some kind of distance limit of Point of Harbor. I just don't know what it is yet.</li> <li>I am thinking Move as One might need to be 1 Essence per packmate, as opposed to just one Essence. Also thinking of adding a roll to the reflexive follow part.</li> <li>And obviously I stole both the Honor and Glory Facets, but the Honor Facet feels a lot more out of place now than it did in the Gift in its first iteration. I might leave it anyway because I am lazy, but if anyone had any ideas that would be fine too. Maybe something with a verge? Or linking one doorway to lead to another?</li> </ul>What do you guys think? <hr /><br /> <b>GIFT OF OPENING<br /> <br /> <u>Modifiers</u><br /> <br /> Bonuses</b><br /> Location is within 10 yards of a Packmate (+1)<br /> Location is under the effects of a Locus (+1)<br /> Location previously visited via Pry Open the Gate (+1)<br /> <br /> <b>Penalties</b><br /> Under the Effects of a Grapple (Opponent\u2019s Strength +1)<br /> Location is not visible (-2)<br /> Location is under the effects of a Wound (-2)<br /> Location is within 10 yards of an Uratha in Death Rage (-2)<br /> Location is outside Uratha\u2019s territory (-2)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>PRY OPEN THE GATE (Cunning)</b><br /> <br /> The Prey has no sanctuary from an Uratha with this facet.<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Manipulation + Occult + Cunning<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Uratha\u2019s Spirit is pulled and dragged in all the wrong directions, and she loses half her current Essence (rounded up). If she has no Essence, she suffers the Exhausted Condition<br /> <b>Failure</b>: The Uratha fails to transport herself.<br /> <b>Success: </b>With a sudden blink the Uratha transports herself a distance of up to her Cunning Renown x 10 yards.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Uratha gains a further +1 to future visits to the area.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>WARD THE WOLF\u2019S DEN? (Glory)</b><br /> <br /> The wolf must have a sanctuary, a den to which he can return and slumber in safety.<br /> <b>Cost: </b>5 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration: </b>1 month<br /> This Facet affects all or part of a single structure, or an area of up to the Uratha\u2019s Glory Renown x 10 yards in radius. Within this area, all attempts to cross the Gauntlet, open a doorway to another realm, or use any other form of scrying window, portal, or otherworldly breach suffer a penalty equal to the Uratha\u2019s Glory Renown. The Uratha becomes immediately aware of any gateway or opening forming in the warded area and may reflexively spend 1 Essence to force a Clash of Wills to close it. Using this Facet at a locus in the area seals it shut for a number of hours equal to the Uratha\u2019s Glory Renown.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>(Honor)</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">No matter where the prey runs, this Facet ensures that they can only cross a threshold if the hunter wills it so.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Essence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 1 scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Something about making a doorway in a building open to another doorway in the building.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>POINT OF HARBOR (Purity)</b><br /> <br /> The Uratha who plans ahead can always return home when things get dicey.<br /> <b>Roll: </b>Intelligence + Occult + Purity<br /> <b>Cost: </b>5 Essence<br /> Action: Extended (5 Successes; Each roll represents one minute)<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Purity renown in days.<br /> The Uratha spends essence to implant her mark on an area or object. Once marked, she can spend another essence to return to her Point of Return at anytime as an instant action. If she spends a turn concentrating, she can gain limited vision of her Point of Harbor with a Wits + Purity roll. An Uratha may have only one Point of Harbor at a time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>MOVE AS ONE (Wisdom)</b><br /> <br /> The Uratha can weave and widen the trails he creates, as well as the trails others leave behind.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Permanent<br /> The Uratha may spend essence to carry one packmate per dot of Wisdom with him via Pry Open the Gate or Point of Harbor. Additionally, when the Uratha\u2019s prey uses a Gift of Opening Facet or other supernatural ability to transport herself through space or realms, the Uratha <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">reflexively spend a point of essence and roll (Wits + Occult + Wisdom) </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">to follow the brief rift to its destination</span></span>. Unless in an area affected by Ward the Wolf\u2019s Den, the Uratha must be able to see his prey vanish to follow the trail it leaves behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 12-27-2015, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T18:23:36-08:00","id":793360,"title":"","content":"Why are you taking 2 gifts from other shadow-gifts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T18:36:18-08:00","id":793363,"title":"","content":"Because I felt like it, mostly. And its probably replacing one of his Auspice affinities so I don't see why it can't overlap. It (Pry Open the Gate) was initially supposed to replace a Facet in the Evasion gift, representing some new, unique way a specific Werewolf's Essence interacted with the Gift. In my headcanon that is perfectly logical and would have satisfied the task of giving a player teleport. Then I decided to make it a whole thing. Then I felt like Ward the Wolf's Den was tailor made for this Gift.<br /> <br /> You can think of Glory in your mind as undecided if you want. Because to some degree it is. My goal is to help my player maintain his character idea. Not presenting a homebrew, just got my hands out asking for help with my game. If anyone likes it as a homebrew that's great, but it's going to be rough around the edges for anyone else's purposes I suspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 12-27-2015, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T05:06:28-08:00","id":801287,"title":"","content":"After a brief read, to me they're ALL teleportation. That's boring. Give teleportation to one of them (Cunning, sure) and then make the others do other things.<br /> <br /> Ward The Den is non-teleportation, but feels like it overlaps heavily with that other gift that protects territory.<br /> Move As One should be reflexive not permanent and also feels like overlaps with the Irraka (?) Share-My-Gifts Gift.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ideas:<br /> Make one social, opening Doors, instead of doors.<br /> Make one about opening metaphorical locks (computers? Keypads? words that sound just like the secret password).<br /> Make one about opening things that normally can't be opened by a single person, e.g. the lock of a canal or a drawbridge or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T07:45:07-08:00","id":804446,"title":"","content":"I would generally warn off outright teleportation as a power for werewolves. You'll note that the closest to it in 2e thus far is the 5-dot Half Moon Facet, which is potent but also very limited.<br /> <br /> If I'm completely honest, I'm not sure that teleportation would particularly fit, thematically, with the concept of 'opening' anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T08:19:41-08:00","id":804466,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. Though, just to be clear, the whole point was specifically to give one of my players teleportation because I promised I would and I'm a man of my word. Thematic or not (I certainly don't disagree), this was just sort of an 'in for a penny, in for a pound' situation. Definitely not intended as a 2e conversion the actual Gift of Opening or even as a good idea for anyone's game. I just chose the name because I always thought it sounded cool. Gift of Gates, Gift of Portals, Gift of Transport, etc. just weren't as fun sounding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T08:32:39-08:00","id":804475,"title":"","content":"I could see something similar to changelings opening portals to the Hedge, where you open a door and it 'opens' to the closest door to the werewolf's sacred hunt prey, maybe?<br /> <br /> One of them sounds like it should flat out open a portal to the Hisil. It would be a breaking point toward the Spirit, and potentially lead to more, but seems to fit the vibe of 'opening.' Maybe have it as a sort of a trap? Like a pit trap in the Gauntlet, so if a target moves across it opens up and sucks them to the other side? Or, maybe, you can just activate it on them, drag them across?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-09-2016, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}